            <profile id="e9be-a8a6-1734-6dcb" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="dab5-785d-be28-f228" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, light armour, and musical instrument. Must have a horse (free) or camel (+12 pts) if mounted. Mounts may have cloth barding (+4 pts). May wear heavy armour (+2 pts) or partial plate armour (+2 pts if mounted, +4 pts if dismounted). Kapikulu. Mehterhane: if used, Mehterhane models must be deployed together and with the Army General; the unit led by the General and including the band is immune to panic, and each Mehterhane model in the unit adds +1" to the Leadership radius of the Army General up to a maximum of +4". If taken, Camels. Ottoman Empire only: 0-4 Mehterhane (0-2 in armies of up to 1,999 pts, 0-3 in armies from 2,000 to 2,999 pts, and 0-4 from 3,000 pts and up; only the maximum of four is enforced). (Vlad the Impaler p.39)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="2bf6-5680-c309-a096" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
