            </profile>
            <profile id="01fa-14ff-b000-a1e3" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="dab5-785d-be28-f228" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon. May have heavy armour (+2 pts), shield (+2 pts) and tirpan, balta, harba, or zipkin (polearms, all count as halberds, +2 pts). Warband. The Imam must accompany the Iayalar. He is subject to Frenzy and confers Frenzy on the unit he leads. Gazi State: one Imam for every unit of Iayalar. Ottoman Empire: 0-1 Imam. (Vlad the Impaler p.39)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="0137-a7af-feb6-f4c6" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
              <modifier type="set" field="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1" value="5+">
                <conditions>
                <condition field="selections" scope="f067-1450-aa49-f48b" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="06c3-79f1-5fff-a4ca" type="atLeast"/>
