  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="933f-c185-d483-42e6" name="Ottomans (Vlad the Impaler) - List Notes" publicationId="dab5-785d-be28-f228" hidden="false">
      <description>OTTOMAN ARMIES (Vlad the Impaler, pp.36-43): the Ottoman Gazi State (1281-1361) and the Ottoman Empire (1362-1526). Special rules from the book: Ditch &amp; Stakes, Gazi, Kapikulu, Mehterhane, Ottoman Artillery, Ottoman Wagon Tabor, The Padişah is Dead! Allies are documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Ottomans - Gazi State (1281-1361)]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: at least 50%
  Infantry: up to 25%
  Vassals: up to 10%
  OTTOMAN GAZI STATE, 1281-1361. Characters up to 25% (one Imam for every unit of Iayalar; no Mehterhane); Cavalry at least 50% (0-1 Timarli Sipahi per 1,000 pts; 1+ Müsellem; 1+ Akinci); Infantry up to 25% (Azab, Gönüllü, or Yaya, no handguns, no Ditch &amp; Stakes; 0-1 Iayalar or Balkan Tribal Warbands per 1,000 pts); Kapikulu &amp; Special Troops: 0-1 Al Manjanik per each 1,000 pts, no other special troops available; Vassals up to 10% (Darabanci only); Allies and Mercenaries up to 25% from the Late Byzantine list - Archers, Kontaritoi (0-1 unit), Mercenary Horse Archers, Pronoia Alagaion (documented only). Gazi: any infantry or cavalry unit may upgrade to Gazis for +1 pt per model (re-roll the first failed Panic test).
[Ottomans - Ottoman Empire (1362-1526)]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 35%
  Kapikulu &amp; Special Troops: up to 40%
  Vassals: up to 50%
  OTTOMAN EMPIRE, 1362-1526. Characters up to 25% (0-4 Mehterhane - 0-2 in armies up to 1,999 pts, 0-3 from 2,000 to 2,999 pts, 0-4 from 3,000 pts; 0-1 Imam); Cavalry at least 25% (1+ Timarli Sipahi; 1+ Akinci); Infantry up to 35% (0-1 unit of Azabs may be armed with handguns after 1429; 0-1 Iayalar or Balkan Tribal Warband); Kapikulu and Special Troops up to 40% (0-1 Kapikulu Suvarileri per first 2,000 pts, and 0-1 per each 1,000 pts thereafter; 0-1 unit of Kesici Silahkarda Musellah may take crossbows up to 1429, after 1429 every other unit may take handguns; 0-1 Solaks may be taken if a Padişah is also taken; 0-1 Al Manjanik or artillery piece per every 750 pts - Sahaloz after 1388; Holonborna, Havayi and Bacalusa only after 1453; 0-1 Ottoman Wagon Tabor after 1470, one wagon per 1,000 points); Vassals up to 50% (0-2 Balkan Horse Archers; 0-2 Tartars; 0-1 Djanbazan/Delis only after 1386); Allies up to 25% (Albanians; Bulgars up to 1396; Walachian Small Host; Byzantines up to 1421 - Archers, Horse Archers, Kontaritoi (0-1 units), Mercenary Horse Archers; documented only).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
